s to  have recently quietly changed the rules  for refugee eligibility around october  14th the government's website switched  from allowing human rights workers who  are in afghanistan to apply to only  those who are already outside of  afghanistan canada is taking the easy  route  it is easy to process people that are  outside of afghanistan trying to process  people in a war zone and in hiding  that's not an easy thing to do  but for those still in afghanistan there  are few safe routes out ibrahimi is  scrambling to help the homeless while  also worrying about his own family  two young children and his wife an  engineer who was completing her mba when  the taliban took over she can no longer  study or work we don't know about our  future we have dark future  ibrahimi and his colleagues have applied  to go to canada but most haven't  received a response  they're still scared that we may be  targeted maybe  we may be questioned we may be  so we need to get out of here but for  now he can't leave and he also can't  stay and work in the absence of canadian  funding  like the afghans he supports left in  limbo as canada and its allies decide if  and how to deal with taliban controlled  afghanistan jeff semple global news  kabul  up next auto alignment the tiny robot  changing the game for prepping the game  painting the lines on a football field  isn't as exciting as the actual game but  it can take a day of painstaking  guesswork yet that's no problem for one  robot at the university of british  columbia it can do all that in just an  hour christa dow looks at the machine  painting a promising career ahead of a  busy sports season  he is a cherished member of the ubc  athletics and recreation department nice  and quiet to work with  doesn't complain  this is robbie the robot a lions keeper  some say is in a league of his own it  takes all the guess work out the lines  are laser straight the circles are  perfect  robbie can do what his human colleagues  do only faster and more consistent the  lines are in the same place every time i  can paint the field probably in about an  hour and a half instead of  four or five hours manually despite  robbie's ability and automation he still  requires constant supervision from his  superior  i treat him like a staff member  he treats me like a staff member  sometimes we don't get along so well but  at the end of the day we get the job  done and we both walk away happy  he is among the first of his kind in  canada arriving here three years ago  from a danish company called turf tank  he cost about 30 to 40 thousand dollars  purchased through a partnership between  ubc and the whitecaps soccer team so the  field is already laid out through gps  technology robbie can paint any outdoor  field in any configuration he runs off a  gps so there's a base station that  receives satellite  information so between those two points  he knows exactly where he is the  precision something the white caps  coaching team relies on what we're  looking for is a very technical side  because our coaches want different  colored lines different specs every day  or every week he does his job  to date robbie is responsible for all  the outdoor grass and turf fields giving  it 110 percent  rain or shine  krista dow global news  and that is global national for this  halloween night i'm robin gill  [Music]  trick-or-treating is not just for kids  at least at the toronto zoo where some  furry friends and some not so furry ones  enjoyed their own jack-o'-lanterns thank  you for watching have a great night  [Music]
 

